{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassFormulaCategorical","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilVanishing","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_times_crossings_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_times_crossings_pos","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L272-L281","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nThe trefoil mass times its crossing count is positive, combining the\nconditional mass positivity with the unconditional crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_topological_mass_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_topological_mass_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L264-L270","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nThe square of the trefoil mass is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.mass_ratio_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.mass_ratio_pos","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L254-L262","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nAny ratio of a positive mass `m` to the trefoil mass is positive —\nthe normalisation `m / m_e > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_multiple_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_multiple_pos","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L244-L252","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nAny positive real multiple of the trefoil mass is positive: every\nparticle mass `n · m_e` (for `n > 0`) is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_cat_mass_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_cat_mass_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L226-L242","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nThe trefoil's cat-unit mass is normalised to one — this is the precise\nsense in which the trefoil is the canonical mass *unit*.\n\nProof: the conjecture says `categoricalMass · m_e_MeV_codata =\nm_e_MeV_codata`; cancel the nonzero factor. This is a genuine\nconsequence, and it is what makes the conjecture a constraint on `T`\nrather than a definition of a free quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_topological_mass_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_topological_mass_pos","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `TrefoilElectronMassConj`).**\n\nThe trefoil's categorical MeV mass is strictly positive.\n\nProof: the conjecture identifies it with `m_e_MeV_codata`, which is\npositive by `norm_num`. The hypothesis is used substantively — without\nit, positivity of an arbitrary `categoricalMassMeV` would need `ρ > 0`,\n`m_e_cat > 0` and `tr_M T ≠ 0` as separate assumptions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_strand_times_crossing_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_strand_times_crossing_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L195-L198","doc":"The torus-knot structural identity `p · q = 2 · 3 = 6` for `T(2,3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_crossing_count_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_crossing_count_pos","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L190-L193","doc":"The trefoil has a positive crossing count: it is a nontrivial knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_crossing_count_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_crossing_count_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L183-L188","doc":"The trefoil braid word has 3 crossings — the three positive letters\nof `σ₀³`.  Matches `QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoil_crossing_count`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_strand_count_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_strand_count_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L177-L181","doc":"The trefoil braid word has 2 strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj.trefoil_mass_eq_m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj.trefoil_mass_eq_m_e","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L168-L168","doc":"The topological mass of the trefoil equals the CODATA electron mass.\nThis is the CAL-1 calibration identification: m_e is the trefoil's\ntopological mass in the QOU framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj.mk","kind":"ctor","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L163-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.TrefoilElectronMassConj","kind":"class","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L131-L168","doc":"**Primary conjecture: the trefoil is the canonical mass unit for the electron.**\n\nStated for **given** data — a Hecke element `T` of the `n = 2` sector, a\nmultiplicity `ρ`, and a cat-unit electron scale `m_e_cat` — all three of\nwhich are *parameters*, so an instance must be supplied against a specific\nelement rather than manufactured alongside one.  The single field is the\nCAL-1 identification: the trefoil's categorical mass in MeV is the CODATA\nelectron mass, i.e. the trefoil is the mass **unit**.\n\nThis is the open physical identification `trefoil ↔ electron`, not derived\nfrom substrate primitives.  A trivial instance is FORBIDDEN per\nAGENTS.md §3b-tax — and, since `m_e_MeV_codata > 0`, the field is\nequivalent to `ρ · m_e_cat · |tr_M T| = 1`, a constraint relating the\nthree parameters (see `trefoil_cat_mass_normalised` below).\n\n**Residual weakness, stated rather than papered over (bean `qou-lo1t`).**\nParameterising blocks the discharge the old form admitted — `⟨rfl⟩` no\nlonger typechecks, verified — but it does not close the class. Given any\n`T` with `tr_M T ≠ 0` one may still take `ρ := 1` and\n`m_e_cat := 1 / |tr_M T|` and prove the field; this was checked and\nelaborates. What that costs an author is real (a specific element, and a\nproof its Markov trace is nonzero) and it is now *visible* — the numbers\nappear at the instance site — but it is a cheat that remains available.\nClosing it needs `m_e_cat` fixed by a definition rather than left free;\nthe corpus has no cat-unit electron scale to point at, only the MeV one\n(`m_e_MeV_codata`), so that is the actual gap.\n\nStatus: PRIMARY CONJECTURE (open, no Lean proof from substrate).\nThe class is left without an instance until a derivation is available.\n@conjecture: primary ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_b3_nf_coeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_b3_nf_coeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L117-L127","doc":"The trefoil e⁻ NF coefficient of B₃ is exactly zero (pulled from\n`TrefoilVanishing`).  This is the algebraic reason the trefoil\ndoes NOT couple to the antisymmetric (β-decay) channel itself —\nit IS the mass unit, not a consumer of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.m_e_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.m_e_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L113-L115","doc":"`m_e_MeV_codata ≠ 0`. Required for the mass formula to be nondegenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.m_e_is_valid_mass_anchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.m_e_is_valid_mass_anchor","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L107-L111","doc":"Any positive mass is a valid QOU mass unit (trivially: if m > 0 then m > 0).\nThis is the structural check that `m_e_MeV_codata` satisfies the positivity\nrequirement for a mass calibration anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_unit_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.trefoil_mass_unit_pos","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/TrefoilCanonicalMassUnit.lean#L103-L105","doc":"The CODATA electron mass is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0}]}